From: Project Luma contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ccci: remove sentinel entries from counted sysctl tables

register_sysctl() supplies ARRAY_SIZE(table) to register_sysctl_sz().
Modern kernels validate every entry, including the old empty terminator.
On the Titan's Linux 7.2 kernel this rejects net/(null), and ccmni_init
exits before registering any cellular network devices. Remove the
obsolete terminators from both tables converted to register_sysctl by
the base port.

This retains the real entries, their permissions, handlers and defaults.
No registration or validation error is suppressed.

---

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/ccmni/ccmni.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/ccmni/ccmni.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/ccmni/ccmni.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/ccmni/ccmni.c
@@ -81,7 +81,6 @@ static struct ctl_table tcp_pacing_table[] = {
 		.proc_handler	= proc_dointvec_minmax,
 	},
-	{}
 };
 
 static struct ctl_table_header *sysctl_header;
 static int register_tcp_pacing_sysctl(void)
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_page_pool.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_page_pool.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_page_pool.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_page_pool.c
@@ -70,7 +70,6 @@ static struct ctl_table devalloc_threshold_table[] = {
 		.proc_handler	= proc_dointvec_minmax,
 	},
-	{}
 };
 
 static struct ctl_table_header *sysctl_header;
 static int register_devalloc_threshold_sysctl(void)
